{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Re-measurement on current `origin/main` `e096a33d3b7` (supersedes the 2026-10-19 census)\n\nThe plan was written against `441ca94f4a8`. Everything below was re-measured today on\n`e096a33d3b7`. The same commands run at `441ca94f4a8` reproduce the plan's original numbers, so\nthe method is sound and the difference is real drift, not a measurement artifact.\n\n### Finding 1 — current state of the `_processors.py` re-export block: **ALREADY REMOVED**\n\nAttestation evidence, measured at `e096a33d3b7`:\n\n- `git show e096a33d3b7:src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` — lines 18-22 import exactly\n  `_bootstrap_genesis_keyring`, `_fold_author_attribution`, `attestation_kind` from\n  `._processors_identity`. These are the three names the plan said should REMAIN.\n- There is **no** `from ._processors_status import (...)` block anywhere in the file.\n- `git grep -c 're-exported for back-compat' e096a33d3b7 -- src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`\n  → **no match**. The `# noqa: F401` marker the plan targets does not exist.\n- AC2 executed as written — an AST scan of all 13 files importing from `._processors`, checking\n  every `ImportFrom` for the 7 names — returns **`VIOLATIONS: none`**.\n- `git cat-file -e e096a33d3b7:tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py` → **GONE**.\n- `status_fold_replay_equivalence` is present in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py`.\n  The DELETE-BUT-MOVE the plan describes has already happened.\n\n**Consequence: the entire processors half of this story is already done. AC2 and AC3 pass on\n`main` today.** The landing change was `374cc2f22b1` (db2c), which went further than its own\nplan described.\n\n### Finding 2 — current state of resolver test-site imports: **67 → 19 sites**\n\n`git grep -n -E '_engine_support\\.resolver|_engine_support import resolver' -- src tests scripts`\n\n| sha | lines | files |\n|---|---|---|\n| `441ca94f4a8` (plan's base) | 67 | 51 |\n| `e096a33d3b7` (current main) | **19** | **15** |\n\n**All 19 remaining sites are under `tests/`. Zero in `src/`, zero in `scripts/`.** db2c migrated\nevery production-code importer, so the plan's \"30 `src/rebar`\" bucket is empty, and its named\nmodule-object sites (`test_replacement_walker.py:46`, `test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py:59`,\n`test_attach_commits.py:397`, `test_close_duration_instrumentation.py:27-31`), the monkeypatch\nstring at `test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py:228`, and `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py`\nare all **already migrated**.\n\n### The remaining population, enumerated by distinct occurrence shape\n\nNot a sample — this is the whole set, regenerated from the grep above.\n\n- **A. Module-level `from ... import resolve_ticket_id`** (2): `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py:29`,\n  `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_transition_pre_status_check.py:14`\n- **B. Function-local `from ... import resolve_ticket_id`** (9): `test_plan_review_gate.py:585,614`,\n  `test_transition_reason_honest_3803.py:73`, `test_completion_verifier.py:460`,\n  `test_sidecar_reader.py:86,105,125,157`, `test_audit_retention_cap.py:41`\n- **C. Function-local `from ... import resolve_ticket_dir_name`** (3): `test_completion_token_recovery_heldout.py:126`,\n  `test_gate_error_sidecar.py:93`, `test_gate_error_sidecar_heldout.py:66`\n- **D. Multi-line parenthesised import** (1): `tests/scripts/reducer/test_ticket_alias_backfill.py:13`\n- **E. Fully-qualified attribute call `rebar._engine_support.resolver.resolve_ticket_id(...)`** (4):\n  `test_compact_sweep_perf.py:54`, `test_compact_trigger.py:52`,\n  `test_completion_sidecar_lock_loss_ab54.py:82`, `test_relocated_store_repo_root.py:240`\n\n### A risk the plan did not cover, found while enumerating shape E\n\nAll 4 shape-E files import only bare `import rebar`. They reach\n`rebar._engine_support.resolver.resolve_ticket_id` as an **incidentally bound submodule\nattribute** — some other import in the chain binds it; nothing in those files does. Rewriting\nthem to `rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_id(...)` is only safe if `rebar._ids` is bound the same way.\n\nMeasured rather than assumed: after a bare `import rebar`, `hasattr(rebar, \"_ids\")` is `True`\nand `hasattr(rebar._ids, \"resolve_ticket_id\")` is `True`. **The shape-E rewrite is safe.**\n\n### Shim and prose\n\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` is a 53-line pure re-export of 9 names from `rebar._ids`\nwith an explicit `__all__`; it has no remaining `src/` importer.\n\n`docs/` is **outside** the AC1 grep scope (`src tests scripts`), so no docs file can fail AC1.\n`docs/bash-migration.md:168` still names the shim and is worth correcting for honesty.\n`docs/archive/tier-e-execution-plan.md:18,77,120,178` also name it, but that file is a historical\nrecord of a past migration — rewriting it would falsify the record, so it stays.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793410376022340412,"uuid":"487d6445-a032-46a3-8ec4-df31fd99871a"}